{"metadata":{"title":"Concurrent Model Selection & Cross-Validation","role":"collectionGroup","roleHeading":"API Collection","modules":[{"name":"SwiftOptimize"}]},"seeAlsoSections":[{"title":"Guides & Tutorials","identifiers":["doc:\/\/SwiftOptimize\/documentation\/SwiftOptimize\/CrossValidationFolds","doc:\/\/SwiftOptimize\/documentation\/SwiftOptimize\/HyperparameterTuning"],"generated":true,"anchor":"Guides--Tutorials"}],"variants":[{"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}],"paths":["\/documentation\/swiftoptimize\/parallelmodelselection"]}],"kind":"article","sections":[],"primaryContentSections":[{"content":[{"level":2,"type":"heading","text":"Overview","anchor":"Overview"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Cross-validation and multi-class classification workflows are embarrassingly parallel: each fold split and one-vs-rest binary sub-problem operates on independent slices of tabular data.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"code":"SwiftOptimize","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" and ","type":"text"},{"code":"SwiftML","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" leverage structured Swift Concurrency (","type":"text"},{"code":"withThrowingTaskGroup","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":") to dispatch multiple fold and class estimators concurrently.","type":"text"}]},{"level":2,"type":"heading","text":"Structured Concurrency Pipeline","anchor":"Structured-Concurrency-Pipeline"},{"syntax":null,"type":"codeListing","code":["           Input Dataset [Features, Targets]","                          │","       ┌──────────────────┴──────────────────┐","       ▼                                     ▼"," Fold 1 Split (Task 1)                 Fold 2 Split (Task 2)","   ├─ Fit Candidate                      ├─ Fit Candidate","   └─ Compute Metric                     └─ Compute Metric","       │                                     │","       └──────────────────┬──────────────────┘","                          ▼","            withThrowingTaskGroup Aggregator","                          ▼","         Cross-Validation Average Leaderboard"]},{"level":3,"text":"AutoML Budgets & Cancellation","type":"heading","anchor":"AutoML-Budgets--Cancellation"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"code":"AutoML","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" deliberately evaluates candidates and folds ","type":"text"},{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"text":"sequentially","type":"text"}]},{"text":" inside its actor, which keeps ordering deterministic and avoids oversubscribing CPU cores with nested parallel fits. Its ","type":"text"},{"code":"timeBudgetSeconds","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" is a soft deadline checked before each candidate and fold; a fit already in progress is not interrupted. Parent task cancellation is honoured at the same checkpoints and throws ","type":"text"},{"code":"CancellationError","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":".","type":"text"}]},{"level":3,"type":"heading","text":"Deterministic Class Ordering","anchor":"Deterministic-Class-Ordering"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"In ","type":"text"},{"code":"OneVsRestClassifier","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", binary classification estimators are dispatched concurrently to maximize throughput across cores. Results are tagged with their class index ","type":"text"},{"code":"(c, est)","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" and sorted prior to storage, ensuring 100% deterministic prediction ordering across runs.","type":"text"}]},{"level":2,"type":"heading","text":"Example Usage","anchor":"Example-Usage"},{"syntax":"swift","type":"codeListing","code":["import SwiftOptimize","import SwiftML","","\/\/ 1. AutoML model selection across Logistic Regression, Decision Tree, Random Forest, and MLP","let automl = AutoML(timeBudgetSeconds: 30.0)","let report = try await automl.fit(features: X, targets: y)","print(\"Winning Model: \\(await automl.bestModelName ?? \"-\")\")","print(\"CV score: \\(report.metrics[\"cv_score\"]!)\")","","\/\/ 2. Parallel One-Vs-Rest classification","let ovr = OneVsRestClassifier(num